// PexClassAttribute is used to tell Pex to generate tests for this fixture.

// Testing Arrays
// Pex generates a large test class that includes assertions for each public method of the class.

// AssumePrecondition.IsTrue is used to mark a precondition. The framework will generate a case for each method if the precondition holds.

// PexObserve.ValueForViewing records the values for a variable in order to display meaningful results in the test explorer.

// PexAssume is a utility class used to express properties of the input parameters to the methods being tested.

// PexAssume.True asserts the truth of a condition. If the condition is false, the test will not be executed.

// Pex methods are used to test each public method of the class. The framework generates parameters for the method based on its contracts.

// For instance, when testing the method Add(int item), each parameter is the element to be added to the array and the return value is the position of the element in the array.

// The contract of the method includes its inputs and outputs. The framework generates test data that fits the contract of the method. The framework also observes and records the status of different elements in the system, to display meaningful results in the test explorer.

// The test data includes inputs and expected outputs. The framework generates test data that fits the contract of this method, which is an input parameter and a return value.

// Pex automatically adapts the test data to fit the contract of a given method. Here is an overview of the process it uses:
// • Pex analyzes the code and the contracts of all the methods.
// • Pex explores each method's contract and generates test data that fits the contract.
// • Pex uses the generated test data to call the methods and observe their behavior as defined by the contracts.
// • Pex writes assertions to verify the behavior of the methods against the contracts.
// • Pex generates test cases for several permutations of the test data, each testing a different value or combination of values defined by the contracts of the methods.
// • Pex includes generated assertions in the test cases and generates the final test methods.
// • Pex creates a large test case, which then executes the methods with the generated parameters.
// • Pex verifies the methods' behavior against the contracts. The test framework includes the results of the test execution into the test explorer, which includes assertion results.

// Assertion failures are reported in the test explorer. Each method is displayed as a separate test case in the test explorer. Assertion failures are reported for different test cases.

// Pex analyzes and generates a large test class that includes assertions for each public method of the class.

