// When you use Moles to isolate a method, the framework generates a class called SCM with a single static field named Mole_<MethodName>, which holds the return value for the method. The return value of the Mole_<MethodName> field is used instead of the original behavior of the method.

// You can replace the original behavior of a static (Shared in Visual Basic) method by using Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Moles.SCM.Mole_<method name>. The Mole_<method name> field allows you to specify the return value of the method. This provides a clean design because you can isolate the method behaviors in the code.

